<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The mech tab: the mechanitor tree, drawn as a tree.

    order 42 puts it immediately after our hospital tab (41), so the census screens sit together in
    the bar: animals, hospital, mechs.

    No defaultHotKey. Vanilla's Mechs button has none either, and inventing a binding is a conflict
    somebody has to go and resolve for no gain. Patch_MainTabsRoot_ToggleTab_Mechs redirects anything
    that asks for vanilla's tab to this one, so a mod that binds a key to Mechs still lands here.

    RimWorld's own tab is suppressed in UIButtonBarConfig.Suppressed when this def is present and
    Biotech is active, so the bar carries one mech button rather than two doors into one screen.

    validWithoutMap is false: every row is read off a map's pawns, so there is nothing to show from
    the world view.
  -->
  <MainButtonDef>
    <defName>Gideon_Mechs</defName>
    <label>mechs</label>
    <description>Every mech the colony commands, drawn the way the system is actually shaped: mechanitors hold bandwidth, bandwidth buys control groups, and a group holds a work mode and its mechs. Bandwidth, charge and integrity are on the screen rather than on a gizmo, mechs that have lost their overseer are listed instead of hidden, and work mechs can be given work priorities the way colonists can.</description>
    <tabWindowClass>Gideon.UIOverhaul.Features.Mechs.MainTabWindow_Mechs</tabWindowClass>
    <validWithoutMap>false</validWithoutMap>
    <closesWorldView>true</closesWorldView>

    <!--
      No file extension and no Textures prefix: RimWorld's ContentFinder takes a path relative to
      Textures and appends the extension itself. Our own Mechanoids icon, which is already in the
      same flat grayscale as the rest of this mod's main button icons and so tints with the palette.
    -->
    <iconPath>UI/MainButtonIcons/Mechanoids</iconPath>

    <order>42</order>
  </MainButtonDef>

</Defs>
